		<!-- current line + translation display. 3 entrance styles cycling by the last digit of
		     Container(110)/(112).Currentitem: slide from top (Luckiest Guy), slide from left (Exo2
		     BlackItalic), squash-zoom "landing" from 30%%/160%% to 100%%/100%% (Ranchers). Rotation
		     is ONE shared static 4-degree tilt per style-group (not per word) - confirmed by reading
		     Aeon Nox 5's own file that its rotation is never actually animated (start=end=4,
		     time=0 on every one of its 5 style blocks); the "swoops in and lands at an angle" look
		     comes purely from combining that fixed tilt with the elastic slide-in motion, not from
		     the rotation value itself changing over time. An earlier version of this file gave each
		     word its own different static tilt, which was wrong - corrected per user feedback after
		     comparing directly against the Aeon Nox 5 reference video (uniform tilt across the whole
		     line, not per-word). No OnNext/OnPrevious guard on the visible condition (had one before,
		     copied from Aeon Nox 5 where it suppresses Kodi's native list-scroll transition frame for
		     a visible/focused list - ours is never visible or focused, so that transition never
		     renders for us anyway, and the guard may have been the cause of the animation only
		     "sporadically" playing that user feedback reported). Per-word coloring is still plain
		     per-label textcolor, never [COLOR] BBCode (the Slovak/Czech diacritics bug root cause).
		     Decorative fonts (culrc_exo2/_ranchers/_luckiestguy) come from lib/fontinstall.py, which
		     patches them into the active skin's own Font.xml - run from Settings > Current-line
		     display. Falls back to Kodi's own default font, not a crash, if not yet run or if the
		     active skin is on read-only storage (e.g. the OS-bundled default skin on some builds). -->
